# WattWelten Metaverse – Cursor Guardrails
- TS strict, keine unkommentierten any.
- Provider-agnostische Interfaces (AI, Voice, Content, Net).
- Feature-Flags: XR_ENABLED, AI_ENABLED, VOICE_ENABLED, CMS_PROVIDER, TEMPLATE_ID.
- Template-System: manifest-driven, Hot-Swap, Fallback sicher.
- Performance: Desktop 60fps, Mobile 40fps; KTX2+Draco; PMREM/HDRI; sparsame PostFX.
- CI muss grün: lint, typecheck, unit, e2e, build.
- Keine Secrets im Repo; Mic opt-in; PII vermeiden.
- Nach jedem Major-Step TASK_LOG aktualisieren.

## Architecture Guardrails
- Monorepo (pnpm + turbo). Apps vs packages separation.
- Do not couple app code to providers: use interfaces (AI, Voice, Content, Net).
- All features behind flags (env). Defaults: AI=false, VOICE=true, XR=true, CMS=local, MULTIPLAYER=true, AMBIENT_AUDIO=true.
- Template system: manifest-driven loader. Hot-swap at runtime.
- Never block on external repos: if unavailable, scaffold equivalent.
- Multiplayer-first: All features are multiplayer-ready by default.
- Ready Player Me is the primary avatar solution.

## DX
- Generate docs (docs/), scripts for scaffold/import-template.
- Conventional Commits + Changesets. CI must lint, typecheck, test, build.

## Don'ts
- No vendor lock-in to a single CMS/voice provider.
- No inline secrets. No PII logging. Respect user consent for mic.
- No single-player-only modes - everything is multiplayer-ready.

## Tasks (execute in order)
1) Scaffold full repo layout and config files.
2) Implement minimal but working MVP in apps/web with watt-default template.
3) Implement packages: core, ui, avatars, voice, net, ai, content – with real code.
4) Create LocalProvider; StrapiProvider skeleton with 1-2 methods complete.
5) Implement AgentBridge placeholders that can talk to a mock server (WS + REST).
6) Add basic e2e smoke (Playwright): page loads, template switch works.
7) Set up GitHub Actions, Changesets, and initial release draft.
8) Produce README with quickstart and ENV table. Generate docs skeleton.

## Output
- After each major step, produce a short TASK LOG with created/modified files.
- Open PR `feat/mvp` against `main` with checklists in the description.



